From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim van der Lippe <TimvdLippe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 08:47:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cargo: Bump crypto-biginit to resolve cargo-deny error
 (#49218)

0.7.5. got yanked

Testing: no behavior change

Signed-off-by: Tim van der Lippe <tvanderlippe@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit e78fc913f26cbd5229cb0f7952b3ea3a4c269236)

----

Fork note: backport of upstream e78fc913f26 (#49218), which landed after
base/2026-10-22. RustSec published RUSTSEC-2026-0387 for crypto-bigint
0.7.5, so `cargo-deny` in `./mach test-tidy` failed on ohos-main. The
commit also takes ctutils to 0.4.5 and cssparser-macros to syn 3.0.4,
which the lock already contains, exactly as upstream.
Drop at the next sync: every later base contains e78fc913f26, so this
commit applies empty and becomes a `Superseded-by: e78fc913f26`
placeholder (runbook decision 3).

Validation: `./mach test-tidy` on ohos-main bf7c1c76aff fails in `cargo-deny` with RUSTSEC-2026-0387 (crypto-bigint 0.7.5) and RUSTSEC-2026-0385 (ctutils 0.4.3), as the Lint job of every pull request would; with both backports it passes, and `cargo-deny check` reports advisories, bans, licenses and sources ok. Same patch-id as upstream (`git patch-id --stable`). With both, on top of patch 130: `./mach clippy --locked -- -- --deny warnings`, `RUSTFLAGS="-D warnings" ./mach build --use-crown --locked --profile checked-release`, the same build with `--ohos` (the Rust part; packaging then stops at the local signing configuration), and `./mach test-unit --profile checked-release` (1,255 tests) and `--doc` (46) pass.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent cherry-picked upstream commit e78fc913f26 without changes and added the fork-style part of this message below the dashed line: fork note, Validation and these trailers)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
